      "provenance": {
        "notes": "The one plant in this batch with possible heart effects: NC State rates the poison medium, says pet ingestion can be fatal (altered heart rate, seizures, death) and gives arrhythmia for people; the ASPCA genus entry (Kalanchoe spp.) lists dogs and cats as toxic with vomiting, diarrhoea and rarely an irregular heartbeat. Graded 3 for pets (the higher of the two readings, rule 5; the 01e baseline was 2 to 3), 2 for children. Seizures have no symptom in our vocabulary and are not listed. Watering: NC State and Clemson say let the soil dry (partly, per Clemson); mapped to let_top_dry. Temperature: NC State 60 F night and 70 F day, Clemson 45 to 65 F nights and 50 to 70 F days. Clemson makes no toxicity statement. Humidity: no page gives one."
      },
